 "notes": [
  "The main trade tables are natural phosphates (HS 2510), gross weight; USGS production is marketable phosphate rock. The tables under them are the phosphate fertilisers and the acid, each its own customs code, gross weight, and none is in the totals of another.",
  "Diammonium phosphate, DAP (HS 310530), 2024 (CEPII BACI): world 18.50 Mt gross weight; top exporters Morocco 6.25 Mt, China 4.25 Mt, Saudi Arabia 3.83 Mt.",
  "Monoammonium phosphate, MAP, and its mixtures with DAP (HS 310540), 2024 (CEPII BACI): world 14.15 Mt gross weight; top exporters Morocco 4.89 Mt, Russia 3.09 Mt, United States 1.72 Mt.",
  "Superphosphates, single and triple (HS 310310), 2024 (CEPII BACI): world 7.84 Mt gross weight; top exporters Morocco 3.54 Mt, China 1.41 Mt, Israel 1.06 Mt.",
  "Phosphoric acid and polyphosphoric acids (HS 280920), 2024 (CEPII BACI): world 7.13 Mt gross weight; top exporters Morocco 3.11 Mt, China 0.71 Mt, Jordan 0.70 Mt.",
  "HS 310310 holds all the superphosphates, single and triple, in one code; TSP, the triple grade, has no code of its own. The Pink Sheet's TSP price is the price of triple superphosphate only: it is not a price of the whole group. HS 310540 holds MAP and its mixtures with DAP. HS 280920 is the acid, a liquid, which the lanes treat as chemical-tanker cargo: the typical class is an Atlas assumption, as for every lane. Other phosphatic fertilisers (HS 310320, 310390) are not loaded; the compound fertilisers, with two or three nutrients, are on the NPK page."
